{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And He appeared to him</b> — adjacent to \"were circumcised\" alongside וירא, teaching that He appeared to him on account of the circumcision. Another interpretation: \"were circumcised with him\" is adjacent to \"and he sat at the entrance of the tent in the heat of the day.\" This is what the Sages said: Abraham sits at the entrance of Gehenna and does not permit anyone circumcised to enter there, except for one who came upon the Cuthean woman whose foreskin was drawn and he does not recognize him." "<b>And YHWH appeared to him</b> — ס\"ת (end-letters) אוה, teaching that He desired to dwell in Abraham's tent." "<b>And He appeared to him</b> — with the words, in gematria: זה בכבוד מילה נגלה אליו (this is in the glory of circumcision He revealed Himself to him)." "<b>And YHWH appeared to him in the oaks</b> — in gematria: לבקר החולה (to visit the sick)." "<b>Sitting at the entrance of the tent</b> — in gematria: להכניס את האורחים (to bring in the guests)." "<b>Heat</b> — four times in the Masorah: כחם היום (the heat of the day); כחם השמש (the heat of the sun); כחם צח עלי אור (hot as the burning heat upon me); ויבאו כחם היום אל בית איש בושת (and they came in the heat of the day to the house of Ish-bosheth). That Abraham sits at the entrance of the tent and does not permit anyone circumcised to enter \"in the heat of the day,\" but rather \"hot as the burning heat upon me,\" which is in the Garden of Eden, as it is written: \"and YHWH will be to you an everlasting light.\" But \"Ish-bosheth\" — meaning one who came upon the Cuthean woman, for there is no greater shame than one who came upon the Cuthean woman — \"the heat of the sun\" shall enter Gehenna, as it is written: \"Behold, the day comes burning as a furnace.\" כחם היום (the heat of the day) — in gematria: זהו בגיהנם (this is in Gehenna), and in gematria: דם מילה (blood of circumcision)."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:16:25.131212920Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}